  "learn": {
    "title": "Crosswalk Controller",
    "body": "Wire green traffic LED on D9, red traffic LED on D10 and blue walk LED on D11, each through its own 220 Ω resistor to the anode and with cathode to GND. Wire a request button from D2 to GND using INPUT_PULLUP.\n\nBegin READY with only green on. A new press prints WAIT, then after 500 ms turns green off and red on. Wait another 250 ms before enabling blue and printing CROSS. After 1000 ms turn blue off and print CLEAR. Hold red for 250 ms more, then restore green and print READY. Track phase and entry time with millis(); never show green and blue together.\n\nRun, press and hold throughout the crossing. The ordered Serial messages are READY, WAIT, CROSS, CLEAR, READY, and a held button must not start another crossing. Release before requesting again. This is a timing exercise, not a certified road-signal controller.",
    "links": []
  },
